eting?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Creative: 15-25 units/week Growth-tier (Reels + carousel + creator UGC + video PDP + before-after wear-test + occasion campaigns). Audience: LAL of subscribers + high-intent perfume interest + occasion + gifting + regional-language segments. Measurement: LTV/CAC/cohort weekly, ROAS by channel + creative + audience, first-purchase vs LTV attribution split, subscription-cohort tracking. In Muscat, Omani + South Asian expat (Kerala + Baluchistan heritage) + East African + Arab expat + Ramadan + Eid + Oman National Day (Nov 18) + wedding season + Muscat Festival (Jan-Feb) + Khareef Salalah tourism inform audience + creative + measurement segmentation."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Common perfume performance marketing mistakes in Muscat?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"(1) Optimising for first-purchase CPA vs LTV (compresses margin over 6-12 months). (2) Low creative velocity (fatigue drives CPL up 30-60% in 60 days). (3) No creator UGC in retargeting (studio content underperforms 20-40%). (4) Weak Meta CAPI (30% attribution loss vs pixel-only). (5) Ignoring WhatsApp CTWA + concierge for premium AOV. (6) Same creative + audience mass + premium + luxury (should segment). (7) English-only creative in GCC. (8) No sampling programme integration in performance ads. (9) Missing IFRA/halal compliance display on landing pages. (10) Not scaling Snapchat in KSA (missing 40-50% of KSA reach). (11) Ignoring wedding + festive concentration (Ramadan + Eid + Oman National Day (Nov 18) + wedding season + Muscat Festival (Jan-Feb) + Khareef Salalah tourism). (12) No LTV/CAC/cohort visibility."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Scaling perfume from OMR 10L to OMR 5 crore/month timeline in Muscat?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"18-30 months well-executed. Key transitions: (a) OMR 10L → 30L: broaden channel mix (add Google + Shopping + PMax to Meta + Instagram core), creative velocity 8-15/week, first LTV/CAC dashboard