      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">Common perfume performance marketing mistakes in Muscat?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">(1) Optimising for first-purchase CPA vs LTV (compresses margin over 6-12 months). (2) Low creative velocity (fatigue drives CPL up 30-60% in 60 days). (3) No creator UGC in retargeting (studio content underperforms 20-40%). (4) Weak Meta CAPI (30% attribution loss vs pixel-only). (5) Ignoring WhatsApp CTWA + concierge for premium AOV. (6) Same creative + audience mass + premium + luxury (should segment). (7) English-only creative in GCC. (8) No sampling programme integration in performance ads. (9) Missing IFRA/halal compliance display on landing pages. (10) Not scaling Snapchat in KSA (missing 40-50% of KSA reach). (11) Ignoring wedding + festive concentration (Ramadan + Eid + Oman National Day (Nov 18) + wedding season + Muscat Festival (Jan-Feb) + Khareef Salalah tourism). (12) No LTV/CAC/cohort visibility.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">Scaling perfume from OMR 10L to OMR 5 crore/month timeline in Muscat?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">18-30 months well-executed. Key transitions: (a) OMR 10L → 30L: broaden channel mix (add Google + Shopping + PMax to Meta + Instagram core), creative velocity 8-15/week, first LTV/CAC dashboard, (b) OMR 30L → 1 Cr: add WhatsApp Cloud API + subscription programme, creator + celebrity, LTV bidding, cohort attribution, (c) OMR 1 Cr → 3 Cr: add GCC/multi-region + trilingual creative + Snapchat/TikTok + Enterprise attribution stack, (d) OMR 3-5 Cr: full multi-channel + multi-region + celebrity + PR + editorial + investor-grade reporting. In Muscat, Omani + South Asian expat (Kerala + Baluchistan heritage) + East African + Arab expat + local ecosystem influence scaling timeline.</div>
